Request Flow

A user signs in through the React application.

The frontend sends authenticated requests to the Node.js API.

The API validates the session, checks authorization, and retrieves or updates permitted records.

When a user requests an analysis, the API creates an analysis job and coordinates processing by the Python service.

Python validates and analyzes the dataset, then stores or returns structured results through a defined service contract.

The reporting service can organize those results into business reports and exportable documents.

The frontend retrieves authorized results and displays them using interactive charts, tables, metrics, and filters.

