24. DATASET FOR INITIAL DEVELOPMENT

Use a real, public sales dataset for the first analytical workflow.

A suitable starting point is the Superstore sales dataset available through Kaggle's dataset search.

Kaggle search:
https://www.kaggle.com/datasets?search=superstore+sales

Before implementing dataset-specific analysis:

Obtain a suitable dataset legally.
Save it in data/raw/.
Inspect its actual columns and data types.
Identify date, sales, profit, quantity, product, category, and regional fields where available.
Document the dataset's limitations.
Build the cleaning and analysis workflow around the actual schema.

Do not assume every version of the Superstore dataset has identical columns.

Do not commit restricted, private, or unnecessarily large datasets to the public repository.

Create a small synthetic dataset for automated tests.

